    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter August 30th with a high-upside lineup, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (70.69) and **Kyle Tucker** (70.33), who remain the core of our offensive engine. **Gunnar Henderson** draws a favorable matchup against Springs, where his score is bolstered by a significant 19% SP Skill advantage and park factors, despite the standard platoon drag. **Kyle Tucker** thrives in his matchup against Valdez, F, maintaining an elite efficiency score despite batting lower in the order. **Drake Baldwin** is a surprisingly strong play today (69.58) as he leads off against Adams, M; his high xwOBA and favorable matchup against a 4.74 xERA pitcher make him a cornerstone of today's scoring potential. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (63.21) provides excellent leverage in the top spot of the order against Matthews, benefiting from a platoon advantage that pushes him into the \"Strong\" start tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Wade Meckler** (38.70), who just missed our 40.0 floor threshold. While **Wade Meckler** offers speed, the combination of facing Wheeler, R\u2014a high-end arm that depressed his projection by 19%\u2014and our current depth meant he couldn't crack the daily lineup. We are also navigating the ongoing absence of **Jordan Westburg**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jacob Wilson**, whose IL stints continue to force us to rely on our bench depth. We are closely monitoring the status of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, as his score sits at a marginal 47.81; he carries significant risk facing the left-handed Suarez, and his platoon drag remains the primary concern for his output today. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (54.15) also faces a test against the talented Gilbert, L, and we will be tracking his early at-bats closely to ensure he isn't neutralized by the high-quality opposition.",
